WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys, I hope you're all
enjoying New York City.

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
Today, it was 45 degrees
and slightly breezy,

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
or as the President
calls that,

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.841
[As Trump] "a national crisis."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:10.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Normal voice ] That's right,
Trump spoke last night

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the border,
and in his speech,

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:15.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trump criticized Democrats,
insulted immigrants,

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:16.216 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and said we need a wall.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:18.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
By the end, anyone playing
a Trump drinking game

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
was like, "Call an ambulance.
Uh...

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:23.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're my best friend.
I hate you."

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.457 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.593
Most people said that Trump
didn't say anything new.

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:29.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
He just repeated what he's
been saying for years.

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:30.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
In other words, Trump's speech
was like

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.800
every phone call with your dad.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Lock your car door twice,
and..."

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:37.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I don't know
if you watched the speech,

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:43.143
but the very first thing Trump
said sounded a little Italian?

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:43.943 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Listen to this.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:49.115
-My fellow Americans, tonight, I
am a-speaking to you.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.818 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:57.323 line:92%
-Can -- Can we hear that again?

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.893 line:92%
-Tonight, I'm a-speaking to you.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.861 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:03.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[As Trump] I want-a
build-a the wall.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:06.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And Mexico will pay the money.

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:08.068 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:11.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's-a right.
It's-a me -- a-Trumpio.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:12.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Normal voice ] Even Anthony
Scaramucci was like,

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.874
[ As Scaramucci ] "Can you
believe this freakin' guy?"

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:15.575 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:18.311
[ Normal voice ] A lot of people
noticed how close the camera was

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:19.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
to Trump
during his speech.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:20.747 line:92%
To put it in perspective, here's

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
how Oval Office speeches
normally look.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.385 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And now here's Trump's.

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.119 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:28.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
They had to crop out
all the resignation letters

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:30.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
on Trump's desk,
I guess is what it is.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:33.259 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.962
But I read that Trump's staff
was very happy with the speech

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:38.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
and thought he was
calm and controlled.

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:39.365 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Then, Melania was like,

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:40.800
[ As Melania ] "I crushed up 20
Benadryls

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
and put them in his food."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.205 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:46.806 size:84% position:42%
[ Normal voice ] I saw
that during the speech,

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:48.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
protesters outside
the White House

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:51.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
held up a giant sign
that said "fake crisis."

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:53.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
Check this out.
Is it -- Yeah.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course, Trump was looking
at that sign

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:57.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the opposite side,
so he was like, "Sisirc ekaf?"

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:01.688 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:04.858 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Adele dazeem?"

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:05.925 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.427 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Well, after Trump spoke,

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:10.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
Democratic leaders
Nancy Pelosi and Chuck Schumer

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.197 size:78% position:39% line:92%
delivered a response.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.900
And a lot of people are talking
about how creepy they looked

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
standing next to each other.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
Check it out right there.
Look at that.

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:19.305 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:19.939 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh, my gosh.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:22.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
They look like extras
from the movie "Get Out."

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:23.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
Uh, they...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]
They look...

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:28.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
They look like two defendants
on "The People's Court."

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:31.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's how your parents look
when you try to tell them

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:34.220 line:92%
about the benefits of CBD oil.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.755 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Chuckling ]
Look at Chuck Schumer.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:40.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
He looks like he's wearing
a Chuck Schumer mask.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Some more news --

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
In a tweet today, Trump
talked about forest fires.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:47.467
But he spelled the word "forest"
wrong twice.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:50.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
Take a look at this. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:51.571 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:52.839 line:92%
I guess you can add spellcheck

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.741 size:78% position:39%
to the list of things
that are shut down.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:56.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like...
[As Trump ] Oh...

00:02:56.276 --> 00:02:57.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
"Forest?"

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:01.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
I spelled "fires" right.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:02.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Normal voice ]
You guys see this?

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
All week, the Internet
has been going nuts

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:07.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
over this app called Twinning,
where you upload a photo,

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:10.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it shows you
your celebrity twin.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, yeah.
So, for example,

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:15.528 size:78% position:39%
if I load this selfie
from my Instagram,

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:18.331 line:92%
I get an 83% match with myself.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.333 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
-83%?
-83%.

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:24.537 size:84% position:42%
-That's pretty good.
-83%, it looks like me.

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:25.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:27.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a weird picture
of me, too.

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:28.441 size:88% position:44%
I don't even remember --
When did I have a beard?

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.109
I have no idea what's going on.
-Yeah.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:32.712
-Well, everyone's been using it,
even some political figures.

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:35.615
I'll show you what I mean here.
First up is Mike Pence.

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:38.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
The app says that his twin
was Eminem.

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:41.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Wow.

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:42.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Cool.
-Yeah.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:45.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Next up, there's
Senator Elizabeth Warren.

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:49.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
The app said her twin was Barb
from "Stranger Things."

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:51.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I miss Barb!

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:53.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-Where's Barb?! I miss Barb!

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:56.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
She should have
her own spin-off.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:58.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here's White House
Chief of Staff, Mick Mulvaney.

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:01.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
His twin was Scooter
from the Muppets.

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Oh!

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:05.311 line:92%
-Up next, there's Eric Trump.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:08.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
His twin was
the bad guy from "Aquaman."

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:10.316 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
And finally,
we have President Trump.

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:14.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
His twin was a yam.
Oh, interesting.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:17.056 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:18.324 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You guys hear this?

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:21.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
Amazon founder, Jeff Bezos
and his wife are splitting up.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:23.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Audience groans ]
But on the bright side,

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
he has a lot of extra boxes
to pack his things up.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:27.900 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
And finally, I heard
that Denver could become

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:34.007
the first city in America to
decriminalize magic mushrooms.

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:35.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're the first ones
to realize

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the only way Americans
will eat vegetables

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:38.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
is if they're also drugs.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:42.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a great show tonight!
Give it up for the Roots!

